{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"How a client proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"text":" — the public-client","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value — was deliberately absent until T21.2: adding it before the rest of the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"understood one would have let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped. The server understands one now (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token.rs"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate_client_credential"},{"text":" has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an arm that accepts ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"text":" credential and refuses a presented one, the authorization endpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derives its PKCE requirement from this enum, and the admin API refuses the method alongside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any grant or binding that contradicts it), so the variant exists — and only that arm may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ever treat a missing credential as success.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClientAuthMethod"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including the records the caller did ask for.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"access. ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carrying an unrecognised value back into an update is refused by the server rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written as a spelling it never used. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over these cases needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arm.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/clientSecretBasic","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/clientSecretPost","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/none","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/privateKeyJWT","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientA